                }
              }
            ],
            "barline": "final"
          }
        ],
        "textAlternative": "The same bar written with two minims.",
        "timeSignature": "4/4"
      },
      "caption": "Better: one minim and one minim. Same sound, clearer to read."
    },
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "text": "Ties are for lengths that no single note can show, and for notes that last across a bar-line. In your Grade 1 bars, look for ties that join two notes you could have written as one."
    },
    {
      "kind": "tip",
      "text": "Ask: could one note value do this job? If yes, use it. If the tie crosses a bar-line, keep it."
    }
